  "id": "COMPOUND:30665 - PROTEIN:5856",
  "verbalization": "(+)-Crassalactone D appears to have a complex relationship with SNU-387, as it is identified as a target of multiple entities that ultimately direct their activity toward SNU-387. The evidence suggests that (+)-Crassalactone D interacts with MIP, which in turn is targeted by two distinct compounds: S-ethylcysteine zwitterion and 5-hydroxy-6,8-dimethoxy-2,3-dimethylbenzo[G]chromen-4-one. Both of these compounds are themselves targets of SNU-387, indicating a potential cascade of interactions where (+)-Crassalactone D may influence the activity of these intermediates, which then affect SNU-387. The shared pathway through MIP suggests a possible mechanism of action, where (+)-Crassalactone D may modulate the activity of these compounds, potentially through direct or indirect interactions. This integrated evidence supports the notion that (+)-Crassalactone D could play a role in the regulation of SNU-387, though the exact nature of this relationship remains to be fully elucidated.",
